# Title, Description, and Thumbnail Guidelines

1. Title Guidelines:
   - Maximum 6 words
   - Must clearly indicate the content range (e.g., "Match Numbers 1-5 with Fruits")
   - Focus on the actual learning content
   - DO NOT include grade level or difficulty
   - Avoid generic excitement words (e.g., "fun", "exciting")
   - Examples:
     ```
     ❌ WRONG - "Fun PreK Number Matching Game"
     ❌ WRONG - "Beginner Fruit Counting Activity"
     ✅ CORRECT - "Match Numbers 1-5 with Fruits"
     ✅ CORRECT - "Count and Add Numbers 1-10"
     ```

2. Description Guidelines:
   - Clear summary of content and learning objectives
   - Specify the exact number/content range being covered
   - Focus on what the child will learn/practice
   - DO NOT mention grade level or difficulty
   - Examples:
     ```
     ❌ WRONG - "A fun PreK level game for learning numbers"
     ✅ CORRECT - "Match numbers 1-5 with their corresponding fruit quantities. Practice counting, number recognition, and one-to-one correspondence through interactive matching."
     ```

3. Thumbnail Guidelines:
   - Show actual content range (e.g., "1 → 5")
   - Display example of the activity
   - Use clear, descriptive heading
   - Include visual preview of learning elements
   - DO NOT include grade/difficulty level
   - Examples:
     ```typescript
     // ❌ WRONG
     <h1>PreK Number Matching</h1>
     
     // ✅ CORRECT
     <h1>Numbers 1-5 Matching</h1>
     <div>1 → 5</div>
     ```

3. Create entry point (entries/index.tsx):
   ```typescript
   import '../../../index.css';
   import { lazy, Suspense } from 'react';
   import { createRoot } from 'react-dom/client';

   // Lazy load components
   const Worksheet = lazy(() => import('../components/[Prefix]Worksheet'));
   const AnswerKey = lazy(() => import('../components/[Prefix]AnswerKey'));
   const Tips = lazy(() => import('../components/[Prefix]Tips'));
   const Thumbnail = lazy(() => import('../components/[Prefix]Thumbnail'));

   // Required type declaration for worksheet view
   declare global {
     interface Window {
       WORKSHEET_VIEW: 'worksheet' | 'answer_key' | 'tips' | 'thumbnail';
       WORKSHEET_METADATA: {
         id: string;
         title: string;
         description: string;
         metadata: {
           grade: string;
           subject: string;
           topic: string;
           difficulty: string;
         };
       };
     }
   }

   const view = window.WORKSHEET_VIEW || 'worksheet';

   const App = () => {
     const getComponent = () => {
       switch (view) {
         case 'worksheet': return <Worksheet />;
         case 'answer_key': return <AnswerKey />;
         case 'tips': return <Tips />;
         case 'thumbnail': return <Thumbnail />;
         default: return <Worksheet />;
       }
     };

     return (
       <Suspense fallback={<div>Loading...</div>}>
         {getComponent()}
       </Suspense>
     );
   };

   // Initialize React
   const rootElement = document.getElementById('root');
   if (rootElement) {
     const root = createRoot(rootElement);
     root.render(<App />);
   }
   ```
   - React initialization and view switching
   - Component lazy loading
   - Global type declarations for WORKSHEET_VIEW and WORKSHEET_METADATA
   - Proper error boundaries with Suspense
   - Default view fallback to worksheet
   - No manual HTML file creation needed (auto-generated during build)



